Related power placeholder patch (0017-houji-drop-placeholder-battery-power.patch):
From: Armada Houji maintainers
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 14:40:57 +0000 (containing commit)
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: omit Houji placeholder power

Houji's firmware reports a constant 10000000 for the translated POWER_NOW
property, independent of the changing gauge voltage/current. Advertising it
causes consumers such as btop to prefer a fictitious 10 W reading. It also
selects their energy-based time estimator although this gauge exports charge.

Do not advertise this unsupported measurement on Houji. Keep the measured
VOLTAGE_NOW and CURRENT_NOW so consumers can derive watts and use the gauge's
charge counter. Leave the property on Qualcomm variants that implement it.

Source: https://github.com/yoni13/armada-houji/commit/cbbb4662865f02fa8375b85ad9ea3738db9d193e
Containing commit author: Yoni Yang <yoni980807@gmail.com>
Containing commit message:
  Fix Houji resume: service sensor DSP requests across suspend
  
  The sensor DSP can send a reverse RPC to the frozen FastRPC listener
  while the AP sleeps. Nothing woke the AP, the DSP watchdog fired, and
  audio, battery telemetry and sensors were lost together.
  
  - fastrpc: wake for successful sensor NEXT2 replies during suspend and
    refuse suspend while a reply is still owed
  - asoc: drain deferred resume before soundcard teardown
  - Game Mode session switch, battery power placeholder, charger suspend
    guard, Gamescope fresh-frame wake, sensor teardown on close
  - README and HISTORY updated; hardware validation notes included

Local adaptation for Aurora:
- Restrict the quirk to xiaomi,aurora while keeping the SM8550 supply descriptor.
- Extend both directions through charge-control threshold reads (wire ID 27).
- Keep charge-control writes (separate opcode 0x48), units and payload sizes intact.
- Translate vendor notification 0x50 into a standard battery refresh, as OEM does.
- Normalize positive discharge current at export, retaining the raw gauge value.
- Use get_property ENODATA for the constant 10 W placeholder, rather than
  adding a duplicate board supply descriptor. Current polarity/sentinel handling
  follows the original Houji export boundary, with the existing Aurora quirk.
- Do not enable ADSP or PMIC GLINK as part of this driver change.

Aurora OEM enum and response layouts:
https://github.com/MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource/blob/c7841217725ac8bed6c4bf790d149dde10444e3d/drivers/power/supply/qti_battery_charger.c

